{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","permalink_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/wireshark:6b5925f...wireshark:c9bd498","diff_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","node_id":"C_kwDOAUV2jtoAKDZiNTkyNWY5YWEzODJhZGFlNTRmNWQ3YzE4MzI5NjljMTU2Njk3MDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T21:48:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T22:40:41Z"},"message":"Workaround LLVM/Clang < 20 __builtin_mul_overflow bug\n\nOn LLVM before 20, on certain platforms, when multiplication overflow is\nchecked for in a way where the width and signedness of the operands\nmeans that a signed 65-bit result is called for, Clang ends up\nrequesting the compiler-rt builtin __muloti4, which is not available in\nlibgcc. There are several shortcuts where there's no problem:\n * operands and result are all the same sign\n * both operands are unsigned and the result is signed, all same width\n * one operand signed, one unsigned, wider operand at least as wide as\n   result. result can be signed or unsigned\n\nCases which don't work (assuming one type 64-bit or larger):\n * both operands unsigned, result signed, widths not all equal\n * both operands signed, result unsigned\n * signed __int128 multiplication\n\nIn the SCSI SBC case, cast the block_size from a uint32_t to a uint64_t\nwhen doing the ckd_mul in order to hit the shortcut and avoid the bug.\n\nIn get_mem_info, memsize should just be a uint64_t, so do that. Linux\nsysinfo has unsigned longs as the operand, Windows has a DWORDLONG,\nand Apple's hw.memsize sysctl is in all practical terms a uint64_t\n(even if the SYSCTL_QUAD macro doesn't appear to enforce signedness,\nApple's own tools use it that way and negative doesn't make sense.)\n\nFix #21744\n\nThis might be easy to accidentally re-introduce, though, if we don't\ntest for this case.\n\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/16778\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/dad9e4a1657b74bc351c1e98ce4774f32fdc77fc","tree":{"sha":"5a9f0a6abbd29fb874d6cddf582ef8833418ba0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/trees/5a9f0a6abbd29fb874d6cddf582ef8833418ba0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705/comments","author":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","node_id":"C_kwDOAUV2jtoAKGM5YmQ0OTgyOGY0ZTljZDhjMDRmOTBhYWNiMTFlMjIzODAxNmJjMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-06T18:11:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-06T21:23:14Z"},"message":"z3950: Use a wmem_array to avoid overflow\n\nSizing the directory array ahead of time can lead to issues when\nthere are partial records, as floor division is used for sizing\nbut a partial record can be added to the array. To eliminate the\nchance of a buffer overflow, use a wmem_array, add each new entry\nto the entry, and then read the count at the end.\n\nThe error handling should probably be cleaned up more, both for\noverflow and for illegal directory entries, but this prevents the\nbiggest issue.\n\nFix #21397\n\nThanks to Anthropic and Ada Logics for the report and PoC.","tree":{"sha":"1f92ef6274efb65a35fcfdd4c3d25cec69cd32bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/trees/1f92ef6274efb65a35fcfdd4c3d25cec69cd32bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/commits/c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/c9bd49828f4e9cd8c04f90aacb11e2238016bc31/comments","author":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events